ASoC: qcom: Fix 24-bit PCM and a crash when the ADSP restarts

Two independent fixes for the Qualcomm DSP audio drivers.

The first makes 24-bit PCM audible: this driver hands the DSP 24-bit
samples in the top of a 32-bit word and calls that S24_LE, so PipeWire's
choice of S24_LE plays silence. It removes S24_LE from what the DAI offers,
which is a visible change for anything that asks for it, though nothing
asking for it can have got the right level.

The second stops an ADSP crash from taking the kernel down. The system now
survives, but the sound card doesn't come back after that crash ("failed to
instantiate card -61"). That isn't fixed here, and the reason isn't known.

Only tested on SM6115, on a Moto G Power (2021).
